{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"9846bbe47631cdd243c9c7f3ad6a22cdb762e54503c04ca186fbf455fd00859a","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"codex:gpt-5.6-sol","buffers":[],"case_id":"a0ae2207bb31d28dc1a32b040177bf9c592e66b7a8ce63c92271601483ec8a4f","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"draw":{"instance_count":1,"primitive":"triangle","vertex_count":3,"vertex_start":0},"entry":"vsInvisible","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"constant-zero-position-observation","output":{"dimensions":[1,1],"index":0,"kind":"render_target","origin":[0,0]},"rationale":"Every invocation returns float4(0) as clip position. The typed position observer is attached, but the degenerate zero-w primitive produces no fragments, so the exact one-pixel framebuffer observation remains the authored poison bytes.","render_targets":[{"dimensions":[1,1],"format":"rgba32_float","index":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urqw=="}],"samplers":[],"stage":"vertex","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"vertex_observation":{"kind":"position"},"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"9898d75c3ca2c32e42da4e17e19e66c87187813bf8ea561a9c66e22b80a82c2a","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"BAAAAAQAAAA=","role":"input"}],"case_id":"82c17c74e57e769fb795dfd58e8f9831201ded546171ed8331b6b921db44b400","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[4,4,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[1,1,1]},"entry":"depth_minmax_down_x2_init","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"gather-depth-quad-lands-inside-one-uniform-block","output":{"binding":1,"dimensions":[1,1,1],"kind":"texture","origin":[1,1,0]},"rationale":"The kernel is straight-line, so execution_safety is loop_free. It gathers the depth texture at pixel coordinate index*2 through a constexpr sampler that reflection reports as coord::pixel, nearest/nearest, clamp_to_edge, and reduces the four texels to float4(min, max, count_below_one, 4). The destination is texture2d<float, write>, which types as R32f, so only the min is observable; dstSize carries air.arg_unused and is never read. The input is four uniform 4x4 blocks -- 0.5 top-left, 0.25 top-right, 0.75 bottom-left, 1.0 bottom-right -- and the case reads back exactly one output texel, (1, 1), whose gather coordinate is (2, 2). Every 2x2 footprint a gather can take around (2, 2) lies inside {1,2,3}^2, so it stays within the top-left block under any of the conventions for which quad a pixel-coordinate gather selects, and min is exactly 0.5 without the case having to assert one of them. What the single value does pin is the addressing: treating the coordinate as normalized would clamp (2, 2) to the far corner and give 1.0, reducing over the whole texture would give 0.25, and being four texels off in either axis would give 0.25 or 0.75. All four block values are exact in binary32 and in depth32_float, so nothing rests on rounding.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[{"binding":0,"bytes_b64":"","dimensions":[8,8,1],"format":"depth32_float","role":"input","texture_type":"d2"},{"binding":1,"dimensions":[4,4,1],"format":"r32_float","initial_bytes_b64":"q6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urq6urqw==","role":"output","texture_type":"d2"}],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"98be56bcdb2fc19a1bd9a5d52792497cdacbc4d6d7ccd50544f2298ff9dfe0d6","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"","role":"output"}],"case_id":"95470251beaa19beb594dea92ed7a9fdb803c88b5796f7dca501a551ca9dc9db","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[32,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[32,1,1]},"entry":"kernel_exact_anchored_math_and_simd","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"anchor-three-transcendentals-where-rounding-cannot-reach","output":{"binding":0,"kind":"buffer","length":1152,"offset":0},"rationale":"Five uncovered families -- air.rsqrt.v3f32 (4 corpus sources), air.log2.v3f16 (4), air.cospi.f16 (4), air.simd_sum.v4f32 (3) and air.simd_shuffle_up.s.i16 (3) -- all asked only where the answer is exactly representable, so every word is a derivation rather than a recording. Each rsqrt argument is a power of four, so the answer is a power of two; that is the guard that matters, because the fast_ roots on this host are not correctly rounded and an exactly representable ANSWER alone does not pin one. log2 sees only powers of two and cospi only integers, where the answer is exactly +-1 -- at odd half-integers Metal returns -0 where MoltenVK returns +0, a signed-zero divergence out of the argument reduction, so those arguments are deliberately not asked. simd_sum is association-proof by construction: every lane contributes an integer and the column totals (528 and 48) are far below 2^24, so any accumulation order gives the same bits, while the lane values still differ enough that summing the wrong set cannot match. simd_shuffle_up with delta 3 leaves the three lowest lanes undefined and those slots are overwritten on a branch over tid, never over the shuffle result. All 288 words were derived in Python before the GPU was asked.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"98ff1876439eab54df2d75e84422372d6239937d52fba7e5c5ac97606aefa821","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"","role":"in_out"}],"case_id":"0f3648ab2220ee8de725bf2f885d72b3fa474e6514e2adb172ebc2d3c9576a26","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[16,16,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[16,16,1]},"entry":"kernel_imageblock_extent","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"imageblock":{"dimensions":[16,16],"implicit_coverage":"full_single_sample"},"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"imageblock-extent-queried-from-every-cell","output":{"binding":0,"kind":"buffer","length":4096,"offset":0},"rationale":"air.get_imageblock_width and air.get_imageblock_height, 17 corpus sources each and both uncovered. Every one of the 256 threads asks for both, so a lowering that answered only for the first cell, or that took the answer from the thread position instead of the tile, would show up in 255 of the 256 rows.\n\nThe imageblock is 16 by 16, the same extent as the threadgroup -- which is the only shape Metal accepts for an implicit imageblock, and the reason the two queries can be answered from the kernel's local size at all. Both answers are 16, and the two are deliberately equal only because Metal will not take a non-square tile here; the two remaining slots are red and blue of the tile cell the thread owns, red carrying the column and blue the row times sixteen plus the column, so a transposed or mis-strided tile moves them even though the extents cannot.","render_targets":[{"dimensions":[16,16],"format":"rgba16_float","index":0,"initial_bytes_b64":""}],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
